  <content_rating type="oars-1.1"/>

  <releases>
    <release version="3.2.0" date="2026-10-24">
      <description>
        <p>Choose your theme, see which collections are left out of the duplicate search, and get your thumbnails back after clearing them.</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Three round buttons at the top of the main menu, and of the menu of the welcome page, follow the system or always use the light or the dark theme. The choice applies at once and is remembered.</li>
          <li>The Left Out button of the Duplicates tab lists the collections left out of the duplicate search, with where each one sits and how many sub-collections go with it, and Include brings one back. The sidebar no longer shows a mark for them.</li>
          <li>After Clear next to the thumbnails in Manage Library, Pigoune makes them again quietly in the background, while you are not using it.</li>
        </ul>
      </description>
    </release>
    <release version="3.1.1" date="2026-10-23">
      <description>
        <p>Show the original of an annotated image in your file manager, and drag images out of a library opened with the folder chooser.</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Show Original replaces View Original: it opens your file manager on the untouched image stored in the library, instead of starting another application that could fail to launch.</li>
          <li>For an annotated image, Show in Files now shows a copy of the annotated image. An image that is not annotated is shown as before.</li>
          <li>Dragging an image out of Pigoune into the file manager works again for a library opened with the folder chooser. The file manager used to show a forbidden cursor.</li>
          <li>A drag whose files cannot be prepared now says so.</li>
        </ul>
      </description>
    </release>
    <release version="3.1.0" date="2026-10-23">
      <description>
        <p>Turn your annotations, resize a text, and leave collections out of the duplicate search.</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Turn a rectangle, an ellipse, a text, a line, an arrow, a pen stroke, a highlighter, a blur or a pixelation with the round handle above it, by steps of 15 degrees while you hold Shift, or set an exact angle with the Rotation setting of the panel.</li>
          <li>A selected text has handles like the other annotations: drag one to make the letters bigger or smaller.</li>
          <li>The spotlight can leave a rounded rectangle lit, steps are bigger and can grow larger, and a blur can go up to a radius of 150.</li>
          <li>A layer is renamed with a double click on its name, or with a second click once it is selected, and its name can be dragged to reorder the layers.</li>
          <li>A collection can be left out of the duplicate search from its menu in the sidebar, and Undo brings it back.</li>
          <li>A blur now hides everything up to the edges of the image. Before, a blur very close to an edge could let a faint trace of the sharp image show through. Images annotated earlier are drawn again without it.</li>
          <li>Files that Pigoune hands to other applications, for an export, a copy or an opening, each get a folder of their own and are cleaned up after a while, and Pigoune refuses a library or a cache folder that is a link.</li>
          <li>Pigoune is quicker with large libraries. The grid and the counts in the sidebar are no longer rebuilt after every import or background analysis, stored thumbnails appear before the original is checked, and dragging many assets out of Pigoune is smoother.</li>
          <li>A library opened with this version can no longer be opened with Pigoune 3.0 or older.</li>
        </ul>
      </description>
    </release>
    <release version="3.0.0" date="2026-10-17">
      <description>
        <p>Capture your screen and annotate it, right inside Pigoune.</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Take a screenshot with Take a Screenshot (Ctrl+Shift+S, the import menu, the launcher icon, or the pigoune --capture command that your desktop can bind to a shortcut), or paste an image with Paste and Annotate (Ctrl+Shift+V). The image opens in an editor inside the window of your library.</li>
          <li>Annotate with rectangles, ellipses, lines, curved or tapered arrows, a pen, a highlighter, numbered or lettered steps, texts with a bubble or an outline, a spotlight, and a blur or a pixelation to hide what is private. Hold Shift for straight lines and perfect squares, pick colors from the image with the eyedropper, choose each tool with a letter, and let the guides align what you move.</li>
          <li>Draw shapes, lines and arrows with a solid, dashed or dotted stroke, and give them a precise, sketchy or very sketchy hand-drawn look.</li>
          <li>Annotations stay editable: the untouched capture is kept next to the annotated image, which is the one shown and exported. Annotate reopens it and View Original shows the capture as it was.</li>
          <li>Layers let you reorder, hide and lock annotations, and the panels of the editor fold away, or hide altogether with F9, to leave room for the image.</li>
          <li>In the detailed preview, hold a button on an annotated image to see the original for as long as you press it.</li>
          <li>Pigoune warns you before you copy, export or open with another application an image whose blur or pixelation is hidden, and refuses to drag it out.</li>
          <li>Copy or export the annotated image as a PNG, or save it in the library, where it receives the capture tag. A capture being edited is kept as a draft if Pigoune closes.</li>
          <li>A library opened with this version can no longer be opened with Pigoune 2.12 or older.</li>
        </ul>
      </description>
    </release>
    <release version="2.12.0" date="2026-10-15">
      <description>
        <p>When look-alikes are not duplicates, you can now tell Pigoune so.</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Ignore Group, in the “⋯” menu of a group, and Not a Duplicate, in the menu of a row, stop Pigoune from offering those assets together. Ignored (N) lists them, Stop Ignoring brings one back, Show All Again brings them all back, and Undo works for each.</li>
          <li>The Duplicates tab is lighter: the trash button only appears once something is ticked, and each group has a clearer title.</li>
          <li>The fine details used to find duplicates now live in their own file in the cache folder, which keeps the database small. If that file is lost or damaged, Pigoune makes it again.</li>
          <li>A library opened with this version can no longer be opened with Pigoune 2.11 or older.</li>
        </ul>
      </description>
    </release>
    <release version="2.11.1" date="2026-10-14">
      <description>
        <p>Pigoune is fast again after the update to 2.11.0.</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Opening a library and Manage Library are quick again, above all for a library stored where files are read through a sandbox portal.</li>
          <li>The background analysis of your assets starts a moment after a library opens, waits while you are using Pigoune, and stops when you open another library. Manage Library shows how far it has got.</li>
          <li>The fine details used to find duplicates are now computed when you first search for duplicates, for the assets that could be duplicates only, with a progress bar.</li>
        </ul>
      </description>
    </release>
    <release version="2.11.0" date="2026-10-14">
      <description>
        <p>The Duplicates tab is rebuilt so that nothing can go to the trash by accident.</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Nothing is ticked for you any more: choose the asset to keep, then tick, one by one, the assets to move to the trash. A confirmation lists exactly what will move, and Pigoune checks every asset again just before moving it.</li>
          <li>Groups only gather assets that all look alike, each marked Identical or Probable, instead of chaining assets that merely resemble a neighbor. Pigoune now compares colors and details too.</li>
          <li>Pigoune analyzes your assets again in the background to learn these details. A library opened with this version can no longer be opened with Pigoune 2.10 or older.</li>
          <li>Earlier versions could offer unrelated assets as duplicates, and Keep This One could send them all to the trash. They stay in the trash until it is emptied or, if automatic emptying is on, for 30 days: open Trash and restore the ones you want.</li>
        </ul>
      </description>
    </release>
    <release version="2.10.1" date="2026-10-13">
      <description>
        <p>Searching for look-alikes is more accurate, and the Duplicates tab is much faster.</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Find Similar no longer offers assets of a very different shape or color, such as a tall wallpaper for a small logo, and puts the assets with the closest colors first.</li>
          <li>The Duplicates tab shows its list at once, loads thumbnails as you scroll, shows a progress bar while searching, and keeps large groups short with a Show More button.</li>
        </ul>
      </description>
    </release>
    <release version="2.10.0" date="2026-10-13">
      <description>
        <p>Pigoune can now find assets that look alike, even in another format or size.</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Right-click an asset and choose Find Similar to list the assets that resemble it, closest first.</li>
          <li>A new Duplicates tab in Manage Library groups assets that look alike, such as the same logo as a PNG and an SVG. Keep the one you want: the others go to the trash, and Undo brings them back.</li>
          <li>Pigoune analyzes your assets in the background after a library opens. A library opened with this version can no longer be opened with Pigoune 2.9 or older.</li>
          <li>A message no longer loses its text when a name contains an ampersand or an angle bracket.</li>
        </ul>
      </description>
    </release>
    <release version="2.9.0" date="2026-10-13">
      <description>
        <p>Asset names can be turned into plain text, and a click next to a thumbnail no longer selects it.</p>
        <ul>
          <li>A new option in Preferences, under Display, makes asset names plain text. A name that is not clickable counts as empty space: a selection rectangle can start from it, and nothing is selected, opened or dragged from it.</li>
          <li>Clicking just outside a thumbnail no longer selects it: the clickable area is now exactly the thumbnail and its name.</li>
        </ul>
      </description>
    </release>
    <release version="2.8.0" date="2026-10-12">
      <description>
        <p>Undo and Redo get their own buttons, the keyboard shortcuts can be changed, and moving assets is clearer.</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Two buttons at the top of the sidebar undo and redo your changes. The message after an undo offers to redo it, and the message after a redo offers to undo it again.</li>
          <li>The keyboard shortcuts can be changed in Preferences, on the new Shortcuts page. Standard ones such as copy, paste and undo are locked, and actions like exporting or importing a folder can be given a key.</li>
          <li>New shortcuts: Ctrl+K adds the selection to a collection, Ctrl+M moves it, Ctrl+T adds a tag, Ctrl+Shift+Z redoes and Ctrl+W closes the window.</li>
          <li>Dragging assets from All or Unclassified into a collection now moves them, and holding Ctrl adds them without removing them from their other collections. Dropping assets on Unclassified removes them from all their collections.</li>
          <li>Adding, removing, favoriting, tagging and moving assets, collections and tags now show a message with Undo, whether you use a drag, a menu or a key. Refused drops explain why.</li>
          <li>Manage Library opens at once instead of waiting for the disk, which was slow for libraries kept behind the Flatpak document portal.</li>
        </ul>
      </description>
    </release>
    <release version="2.7.0" date="2026-10-11">
      <description>
        <p>Choose from 294 icons for your collections, sorted by theme, and enjoy a faster, steadier Pigoune.</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Collections now offer 294 icons in 13 themes, with a search field to find one quickly. Collections you already customized keep their look.</li>
          <li>Searching, filtering and the sidebar counts are several times faster on large libraries.</li>
          <li>Marking a favorite, adding a tag or renaming an asset no longer rebuilds the grid: your scroll position and selection stay put.</li>
          <li>The records in Manage Library now show their thumbnails at once.</li>
          <li>The collection icons come from Phosphor Icons, credited in the About dialog.</li>
          <li>Libraries stay compatible with older versions, but a collection with one of the new icons shows a gray folder in Pigoune 2.6.1 and earlier.</li>
        </ul>
      </description>
    </release>
    <release version="2.6.1" date="2026-10-10">
      <description>
        <p>A fix for a crash when dragging assets over the tags.</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Pigoune no longer closes when you hold dragged assets over a tag with sub-tags, then move the pointer out of the tag list.</li>
        </ul>
      </description>
    </release>
    <release version="2.6.0" date="2026-10-10">
      <description>
        <p>A finishing release: simpler tag navigation, accurate counts, wider image support and much faster deletion of large selections.</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Clicking a tag now shows it and opens its sub-tags at once, and holding dragged assets over a tag with sub-tags for a second opens that level so you can drop them deeper.</li>
          <li>The numbers beside tags and collections follow the search and the filters, and tags with no match are dimmed.</li>
          <li>HEIC photos can be imported when your system can decode them, and unusual ICO, BMP, AVIF and SVG files are recognized more reliably.</li>
          <li>Deleting a large selection is much faster, and SVG files built to exhaust memory are refused.</li>
          <li>Show in Files and Move to for collections join menus that are now ordered the same way everywhere.</li>
          <li>Keyboard and screen reader access to the preview and the tags is better, and a failed export says what went wrong.</li>
        </ul>
      </description>
    </release>
    <release version="2.5.0" date="2026-10-09">
      <description>
        <p>Tags can now be nested, the library can check its own health, and the interface uses one consistent vocabulary.</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Nest tags like Subject › Animals › goat: type a path with a slash, browse the tags level by level in the sidebar, and move, merge or delete a tag together with its sub-tags.</li>
          <li>The new Health tab of Manage Library finds missing, damaged and unrecorded files, and lets you add, replace, remove or trash them.</li>
          <li>Export the whole library as folders, and import images dragged straight from a web browser.</li>
          <li>The search field shows where it searches, and a magnifier opens the search in narrow windows.</li>
          <li>The French interface now says “élément” instead of “ressource”, with the same wording in the other languages, and Manage Library is laid out in a centered column.</li>
          <li>Libraries opened with Pigoune 2.5 can no longer be opened with older versions.</li>
        </ul>
      </description>
    </release>
    <release version="2.4.0" date="2026-10-07">
      <description>
        <p>A short window now tells you what is new after each update, and clearing the thumbnails moves to the library information.</p>
        <ul>
          <li>A short window sums up the main news the first time a new version starts. You can turn it off in the Preferences.</li>
          <li>Clearing the thumbnails is now done in the Storage tab of the library information, next to the space they take, instead of in the Preferences.</li>
        </ul>
      </description>
    </release>
    <release version="2.3.0" date="2026-10-07">
      <description>
        <p>Much faster on large libraries, a clearer wallpaper window and shorter, simpler tags.</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Opening a library and searching are several times faster, and scrolling through thousands of thumbnails stays smooth, even before they have been created.</li>
          <li>A tag is now a single word of up to 20 characters: a space ends the tag you are typing and a hyphen joins several words. Existing tags are left as they are.</li>
          <li>The wallpaper framing window is rearranged around the virtual screen, with a discreet note when the image will look blurry.</li>
          <li>Long names are shortened instead of stretching the panels, and the windows fit the narrowest size even with larger text.</li>
          <li>The search finds œ and æ when you type oe and ae, and exporting can no longer ask for a size that would crash Pigoune.</li>
          <li>Pigoune now tells you when an image cannot be loaded and when links were ignored while importing a folder.</li>
        </ul>
      </description>
    </release>
    <release version="2.2.0" date="2026-10-06">
      <description>
        <p>Turn your images into wallpapers, framed exactly the way you want.</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Frame an image on a virtual copy of your screen, under the bars of your desktop, and set it as your wallpaper.</li>
          <li>Fill the empty space with a color of the image, a gradient, a blur or a mosaic, and darken or mirror the image if you wish.</li>
          <li>Filter assets by shape and keep only the images that fit your screen, also in smart collections.</li>
          <li>Libraries opened with Pigoune 2.2 can no longer be opened with older versions.</li>
        </ul>
      </description>
    </release>
    <release version="2.1.0" date="2026-10-06">
      <description>
        <p>Pigoune speaks more languages and looks the same everywhere.</p>
        <ul>
          <li>The interface is now available in German, Spanish, Brazilian Portuguese, Italian, Dutch and Polish.</li>
          <li>Choose the language of Pigoune in the preferences, or keep the one of your system.</li>
          <li>The icons of Pigoune are the same on every distribution.</li>
        </ul>
      </description>
    </release>
    <release version="2.0.0" date="2026-10-06">
      <description>
        <p>A fresh look for the sidebar, the details and the preview, collections with their own icon and color, and a search by color.</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Each collection can have its own icon and color.</li>
          <li>Filter assets by their main colors, or by any color you pick.</li>
          <li>The sidebar folds its sections and shows tags as pills.</li>
          <li>The details panel is organized in foldable sections, with quick actions and the detected colors.</li>
          <li>The preview zooms in from the thumbnail, shows a strip of thumbnails and can show the details panel next to the asset.</li>
          <li>The library information and the preferences are organized in tabs.</li>
          <li>Libraries opened with Pigoune 2.0 can no longer be opened with older versions.</li>
        </ul>
      </description>
    </release>
    <release version="1.6.1" date="2026-10-05">
      <description>
        <p>Update notices and smoother organizing.</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Pigoune tells you when a new version is available and installs it in one click.</li>
          <li>Creating a collection can now be undone.</li>
          <li>A rename in the details panel is confirmed by clicking anywhere else, and the full name appears when it is shortened.</li>
          <li>The shortcuts window lists the keys of the sidebar, and a few preferences are worded more clearly.</li>
        </ul>
      </description>
    </release>
    <release version="1.6.0" date="2026-10-05">
      <description>
        <p>Smart collections, richer searches and more preferences.</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Create smart collections that fill themselves with the assets matching your words, types and favorites.</li>
          <li>Search several words at once: words joined by “and” must all be found, words joined by “or” are alternatives.</li>
          <li>The search shows where it looks and how many assets it found.</li>
          <li>New preferences: thumbnail background, format badges, double-click to open, search the whole library, and showing or hiding tags and smart collections in the sidebar.</li>
          <li>The details panel keeps the same width whatever the selected asset.</li>
          <li>Libraries opened with Pigoune 1.6 can no longer be opened with an older version, so update Pigoune on all your computers.</li>
        </ul>
      </description>
    </release>
    <release version="1.5.1" date="2026-10-04">
      <description>
        <p>Pigoune now has its own website and updates itself.</p>
        <ul>
          <li>The About window links to the new website of Pigoune.</li>
          <li>Pigoune installed from its website updates itself through Software.</li>
        </ul>
      </description>
    </release>
    <release version="1.5.0" date="2026-10-04">
      <description>
        <p>Libraries ready to grow, and their real location shown in Flatpak.</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Assets are now sorted into small subfolders inside a library, so very large libraries stay easy to handle for file managers, backups, sync tools and USB drives.</li>
          <li>The welcome page, the recent libraries and the library information show the real folder of a library instead of a technical path.</li>
          <li>Libraries opened with Pigoune 1.5 can no longer be opened with an older version, so update Pigoune on all your computers.</li>
        </ul>
      </description>
    </release>
    <release version="1.4.0" date="2026-10-04">
      <description>
        <p>A big update, with new formats, conversion and a closer look at your libraries.</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Import AVIF, JPEG XL, TIFF and BMP images, and play animated PNG and WebP images.</li>
          <li>Pause an animation in the preview and step through it frame by frame.</li>
          <li>Export assets converted to PNG, JPEG, WebP, AVIF or ICO, with size, quality, background and multi-size icons.</li>
          <li>See the key figures of a library, a chart of the space used by each format, its disk space and its records.</li>
          <li>Reopen recent libraries from the main menu or the welcome page.</li>
          <li>Choose whether to reopen the last library, play animations on hover and how many recent libraries to keep, and clear the thumbnails.</li>
          <li>Libraries opened with Pigoune 1.4 can no longer be opened with an older version, so update Pigoune on all your computers.</li>
        </ul>
      </description>
    </release>
    <release version="1.3.0" date="2026-10-04">
      <description>
        <p>Take a much closer look at your assets in the detailed preview.</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Move between assets with on-screen arrows, a two-finger swipe, Home and End.</li>
          <li>See the format, dimensions and size of the shown asset.</li>
          <li>Drag the image freely, zoom with new buttons, and fill the screen with F11.</li>
          <li>Spot the real edges of an image and, from 800%, every single pixel.</li>
          <li>Star, copy, export or open the shown asset without leaving the preview.</li>
          <li>Switch between the sizes stored in an ICO file.</li>
          <li>Open any asset in another application with Open With.</li>
          <li>Grab the window more easily by the middle of the library header.</li>
        </ul>
      </description>
    </release>
    <release version="1.2.1" date="2026-10-03">
      <description>
        <p>Stop the thumbnail grid from flickering while the window is resized.</p>
      </description>
    </release>
    <release version="1.2.0" date="2026-10-03">
      <description>
        <p>Give the thumbnail grid a cleaner look.</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Thumbnails sit in square frames, evenly spaced across the whole width.</li>
          <li>Favorites show a larger yellow star that grows with the thumbnails.</li>
          <li>A new preference hides the names under the thumbnails.</li>
          <li>Small images stay sharp, and the lasso shows the selection while it is drawn.</li>
        </ul>
      </description>
    </release>
    <release version="1.1.0" date="2026-10-03">
      <description>
        <p>Add a user guide, available from the main menu or with F1.</p>
      </description>
    </release>
    <release version="1.0.0" date="2026-10-03">
      <description>
        <p>The first public version of Pigoune.</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Import SVG, PNG, JPEG, WebP, GIF and ICO files, or whole folders, with duplicate detection</li>
          <li>Organize assets with nested collections, tags, favorites, notes and credits</li>
          <li>Find any asset instantly with search and filters</li>
          <li>Preview assets up close, animated GIFs included</li>
          <li>Reuse assets by dragging, copying or exporting them</li>
          <li>Undo changes and restore assets from the trash</li>
        </ul>
      </description>
    </release>
  </releases>
</component>
